WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 8 - Into the Wind

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.700
Seijouchuu Academy

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.240
Purple roses...

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.280
My first fan!

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.860
I wonder what kind of person my fan could be?

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.190
I looked at the roses every day until they wilted,

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:00.530
and then had one of them pressed.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.910
Thank you, Mr. or Mrs. Purple Rose!

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.910
Kitajima!

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.230
Kitajima!

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.180
Yes!

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.000
Pay attention!

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.120
Give me the primary formula for factorization!

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.500
What? A formula?

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.530
Well...

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.640
Can't you even remember a simple formula?!

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.760
Hey, did you watch the made-for-TV special last night?

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.570
It made me cry!

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.630
In the end, the police arrive at the cliff and then....

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.340
when she hears them, the criminal's mother turns to the policeman and says:

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:39.650
"Officer, wait! She didn't do it... <i>I</i> did!"

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.880
"Don't, Mom! Officer, my mom had nothing to do with it! I committed the crime!"

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.800
"Sanae, you don't need to protect me."

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.700
"But, Mom! You're doing this for me!"

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.080
"Go find your happiness, Sanae."

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.000
"<i>Mom!</i>"

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.230
What a strange girl.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.120
She can't remember a formula to save her life, but she can recite...

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.810
an entire show after seeing it just once.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.050
Maya, bad news.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.120
Take a look at this magazine!

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.040
A Former Great Actress:  <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.650
Chigusa Tsukikage has formed a new acting troupe in an effort to train...

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:46.530
the next lead actress for lost masterpiece, <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.470
Her undisclosed affiliation with the President of Aoyagi Productions...

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.760
On this page, they're even going as far as suggesting that...

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.870
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe's debut, <i>Little Women</i> was a poor production,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.920
notable only for the fact that the stage was ruined by the inexperienced acting.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.130
It was a resounding failure.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.990
All the critics are saying the same.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.640
The stage... was ruined?

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.760
How can they say it was a failure when we've worked so hard to perform it?!

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:23.310
Ma'am, is this really true?

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.470
Was our acting that bad?

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.830
Did you really form this troupe for the sole purpose of training...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.420
the next Scarlet Angel?!

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.900
Just how closely <i>are</i> you involved with the President of Aoyagi Productions?

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.830
I want you all to calm down!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.400
These are nothing but malicious rumors!

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.110
Ruinous slander perpetrated by someone bent on destroying my troupe!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.880
What kind of fictitious article is this, anyway?!

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.050
Mr. Aoyagi is not my patron at all!

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.050
Which is more than I can say for the writer of this review!

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.120
We received nothing but praise from those who actually bothered to come and watch our show!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.620
Hello?

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.940
He's the only one who could be behind this...

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.830
Don't worry! You have no reason to pay even the slightest attention...

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.970
to an article like that...

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.630
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.510
She needs to rest now.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.640
Please, go on home now.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.250
I didn't realize she had a weak heart.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:46.470
If we hadn't gotten so worked up, maybe this wouldn't have happened.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:50.470
But what's going to happen to us from here on out?

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.310
I guess I really don't have any talent after all...

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.510
From that day on, there was a subtle shift in the mood of the Tsukikage Acting Troupe.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.250
Are you really quitting?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.270
Yes. I mean, how can I look my friends in the eye after a review like that?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.180
I'm going to look for a new troupe.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.880
Now, wait just a minute!

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:19.440
It's not like we blame Ms. Tsukikage, but after this whole scandal business,

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.760
we're just hurting our own careers by staying here.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.480
You guys should think about that too.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.730
Our parents...

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:30.240
also told us we shouldn't work with a tutor who has a sponsor.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.550
Her plan is to train the next Scarlet Angel.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.630
There's no reason for guys to stick around if that's the case.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.050
Ten people have already quit. It's getting pretty lonely around here.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.240
She's probably mad...

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.960
I mean, I've skipped work twice to go to rehearsals without even telling her.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.790
Maya!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.370
I'm so sorry!

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.230
It will never, ever happen again, so please don't fire me!

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.610
What are you talking about?

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.060
You've always sent someone in to cover your shifts.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.310
Here you go!

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.100
Sakurakouji!

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:26.600
Maya!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:28.650
So, what do you think?

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.200
I look pretty good in this, don't I?

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.330
Sakurakouji.... thank you so much!

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.290
Maya...

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.140
Hey... everyone's looking at us.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.180
Maya...

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.300
What possessed me to just throw myself at him like that?!

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.120
He must be angry at me.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.800
Your boyfriend's a hunk!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.300
My boyfriend?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.900
They made you a knight in the school play?

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.740
Yeah. That's the script.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.620
I'd love to be in this play!

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:15.620
"Julia, I have neither land, nor name, nor inheritance..."

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:19.560
"But when it comes to my love for you, I have more than enough!"

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:24.310
"Stop that, Alex. If my father finds out we've been meeting like this..."

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:31.010
"Julia, please don't go! I've been drawn to you since the first day I met you!"

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:35.320
"Tell me that you love me too!"

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:40.110
"The way you smile, the way you move..."

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.090
"There's nothing about you that I'm not comfortable with!"

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:49.030
"Since I first met you, I can't get you out of my head."

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:55.340
"My one and only hope is to be with you - to love you and to be your strength."

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.680
And then?

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.350
No... let's stop there.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:05.440
I wonder what made him clam up all of the sudden.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.840
He's acting strange.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:14.770
If only she paid half as much attention to me as she does to acting...

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.210
Masumi Hayami.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:31.030
It's too late to withdraw that article now.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.800
I have no involvement with Mr. Aoyagi, but I have borrowed money from him in the past.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.990
That much is true.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.510
And then... <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>...

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.710
Please come in.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.300
How are you feeling, ma'am?

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:50.760
I've made you all worry about me, but I'm better now.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.370
I'm going out to buy a few things.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.270
Thank you.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.200
Scoop

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.680
You really shouldn't pay any attention to that magazine.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:08.040
Masumi Hayami bribed a handful of critics to write it.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.970
You all acted superbly.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:14.290
Masumi Hayami? Of the Daito Troupe?

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:15.960
But why would he do something like that?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.720
He's...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:24.520
He's convinced that Aoyagi Productions and our troupe have joined forces...

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.750
and are now a threat to his business.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.760
He wanted to destroy our troupe as quickly as possible.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:35.350
He's a man who believes the end justifies the means.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.760
He does? I don't believe it...

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:43.690
Rumors are forgotten if you give them enough time.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:47.150
You'll have to become mentally strong as quickly as you can so that you don't fold...

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.770
to these kinds of dirty tactics.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.430
You're in the Tsukikage Acting Troupe, right?

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.570
Yes, sir.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.830
Can you show me the way to your tutor's room please?

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.050
What?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.630
But you can't go see her right now!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.850
She's still ill and...

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:31.660
There is no need for violence!

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:34.680
If you wish to speak to me, you may do so in here.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.800
Come in.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.190
But ma'am, you're still not well enough to...

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.350
Ma'am...

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.530
What kind of an article do you call this?!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.550
We can silence any talk about your dealings with our president,

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.810
but what's this review about?

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.050
What are you teaching these kids?!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.310
Our president is beside himself with anger!

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.760
That review isn't accurate.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.710
Whether it's accurate or not is beyond the point!

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:07.740
Its very existence has caused us to lose credibility!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.790
Our company has only recently entered show business and yet,

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.840
every movie and TV show we have financed has prospered!

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:18.840
It's got to a point where all new productions only stand a chance...

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.340
if one of our stars is in it.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.720
Our interest in gaining a foothold in the theater business as well...

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.810
has already led us to finance you to the tune of three-hundred million yen!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.020
Three-hundred... million?

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.430
You need to hurry up and produce stars: for commercials,

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.720
for TV, for the film industry and for the stage, so that they can earn all that money back!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:35.260
How are you going to produce stars with a review like this?!

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:42.270
How will you pay off your three-hundred million yen debt if you can't produce stars?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.350
Then, tell me what you want me to do.

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:53.130
The National Japanese Acting Federation will be staging their very first nationwide competition next year.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.540
Regional preliminaries begin at the start of the year.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.130
In spring, the troupes who make it to the finals in Nagoya...

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:02.370
will participate in a three-day competition.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:06.960
The winning troupe will gain fame as Japan's number one acting troupe.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:10.760
As you can imagine, lots of troupes and academies will be participating.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.080
We want your troupe to participate too, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.690
You want the Tsukikage Acting Troupe to enter this competition, win it,

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:19.280
and erase all the bad publicity surrounding us?

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:23.050
We want you to win.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.620
Or if that's not possible: at least make the top three,

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.150
as they will be featured on television.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:30.510
It doesn't sound like I have much choice.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:34.650
Do you understand how important this competition is...

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.980
to the future of the Tsukikage Acting Troupe?

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:43.010
If you not only fail to repay the three-hundred million used to finance this venture,

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:46.660
but also fail to clear the black mark on your name,

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:50.000
we shall have no other choice but to disband the Tsukikage Acting Troupe.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:54.020
Disband... the troupe?

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:59.500
Acting Competition
Tokyo District Preliminary
Admissions Office

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:08.670
Look... that's the Tsukikage Troupe - they were talked about in that magazine...

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.530
Oh, you mean that scandal?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.150
The critics said their debut was a complete disaster!

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:15.440
Don't tell me they're actually entering!

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.190
Oh well, they won't even make it past the first round.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.760
It'll be fun to see how bad they are though!

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:23.100
Rei, Maya. Go wait for me in the car.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.250
Let's go.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:30.030
Well, well, I didn't expect to see you here, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.810
Hey, that's Masumi Hayami from the Daito Troupe!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:38.160
So your troupe is entering the competition too, I assume?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:43.160
Just make sure that your piece isn't labeled a train wreck again!

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:46.510
I wanted to thank you, Masumi.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:50.630
Because you tore my group apart so thoroughly,

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:54.760
if we win this competition, we'll get even more national attention.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.630
Nice to see you too.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:01.240
But those reviews were written by professional critics.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.890
They had nothing to do with me.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.890
But their opinion is valuable.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:10.380
After all, their views influence the way the public views the theater.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:14.380
It seems that opinion regarding the Tsukikage Acting Troupe has already been set in stone.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:26.040
I can't say I didn't enjoy killing a couple of hours at your last show.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:33.800
Maya!

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:38.310
I was worried about your health, so I came back to get you...

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.220
Just remember this, Masumi.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:45.890
I will never kneel to you. Never.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.550
I would sooner die.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.750
And I will fight you to the bitter end.

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:54.920
Then I will consider that a formal challenge aimed at the Daito Troupe...

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.500
and our very own Ondine Troupe too.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.990
Right then.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:01.010
We shall meet again in the acting competition.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:04.090
Yes. We'll meet face-to-face, head-to-head.

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:05.850
Maya, let's go.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.670
Please give that back!

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.720
It has great sentimental value!

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:18.670
It does?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:22.590
After we performed <i>Little Women</i>,

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.990
I received a big bouquet of purple roses from a fan.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.050
A fan, you say...

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.950
I have no idea who sent them to me.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.740
Isn't it a bit strange that I was given flowers?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.800
But it made me so happy.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:42.520
Nothing like that has ever happened to me before... and it gave me strength!

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.340
That's why I've pressed it and why I keep it on me at all times.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.470
What's so funny?!

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.050
Nothing.

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:54.490
I'll give it back to you then, if you treasure it so much.

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:02.880
Purple roses...

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:08.840
Oh... I never thought someone like Masumi Hayami would laugh like that!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:24.510
I can't say I didn't enjoy killing a couple of hours at your last show.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:30.580
I've finally understood just how low that man will sink for his business!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:32.770
He's a cruel, heartless man!

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.070
We won't back down.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.180
No matter how strong the wind blows, you keep on walking, standing tall.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.100
I won't back down.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:44.250
No matter how hard the wind blows, I'll face it head on.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:51.890
I've decided on the piece we will be doing for the Tokyo District Preliminaries.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:54.960
We will perform Ichiyo Higuchi's <i>Takekurabe</i>.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.310
I will now hand out the roles.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:00.180
The lead role, Midori, will be played by Maya Kitajima.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:02.900
Next, Shinyo...

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:04.110
Hold on a minute!

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.380
I can't do that!

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:09.440
I could never play a lead role in something this important!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:13.930
Ms. Tsukikage has picked you <i>because</i> it's so important!

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:19.670
But I'm in Class C... and I have practically no experience either.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:25.340
Is there anyone who objects to Maya taking the lead role?

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:29.630
If anyone can do this, it'll be Maya...

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:30.840
Yeah!

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:33.630
Go on, take it! You can do it!

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.340
Just try your best and I'm sure you'll manage just fine!

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.340
Congratulations, Maya!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.230
You'll be fine! Congrats!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.080
This is great, isn't it, Maya?

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.140
We're counting on you!

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:46.610
What's wrong?

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:53.610
I don't know exactly, but all this time, I've never been good at anything...

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:57.580
I was never good in school and yet, everyone is so kind...

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:03.350
telling me I can do this. It just makes me so happy.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.130
Don't be silly!

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:09.640
You won't contest the decision this time, will you, Sayaka?

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:12.520
No. I know she can do it.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:17.310
After all, she has more raw talent than anyone else here.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:21.060
But she hasn't figured that out for herself yet.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:27.170
Just look at all of them. Since her performance as Beth, everyone respects her...

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:30.260
as an actress with much more talent than themselves.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.790
I'm back!

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:37.050
Welcome home.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:37.840
Here you go...

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:40.330
Takekurabe

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:51.740
You know, the main character Midori is close to your own age.

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.280
She's also a fourteen-year-old girl.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:54.070
I see.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:57.170
The story takes place at the beginning of the Meiji period in Yoshiwara.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.770
Midori is a rich, beautiful and competitive girl.

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.150
All the young men desire her.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:06.660
Rich... beautiful... competitive...

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:10.500
She secretly loves a temple boy named Shinyo,

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.040
but she can't bring herself to confess her true feelings to him.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:17.800
Shinyo loves her as well, but he can't help but give her the cold shoulder.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:21.330
And then, tragedy strikes.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.230
This is a story of adolescence that resonates with boys and girls everywhere,

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.030
no matter what era they live in.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:32.090
But I don't have any of those things... I'm not beautiful nor rich...

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.010
and I don't attract the attention of young men.

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.710
That's fine though. That's what acting is all about, right?

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:40.240
You're right! That <i>is</i> what acting is all about!

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:41.670
I can become her on stage!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.530
I can become Midori on stage!

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:47.220
Acting's fantastic because it allows you to become all sorts of people!

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:53.600
I will now announce our play for the Tokyo District Preliminaries.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:58.340
The play will be... Ichiyo Higuchi's <i>Takekurabe</i>.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.720
The part of Shinyo will be played by Sakurakouji.

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:08.610
The lead role, Midori, will be played by Ayumi Himekawa.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.620
I will become Midori from <i>Takekurabe</i>.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:20.630
I'll do it.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:24.030
No matter what happens, I'm going to stay strong; I'll show them all.

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:28.430
That's all I have - acting is all I have!

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:35.600
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe has no idea that the Ondine Troupe will be performing the same play as them.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:40.920
This is all part of Hajime Onodera's cowardly plan.

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:45.310
If they don't win, the Tsukikage Acting Troupe will fold.

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:49.510
What sort of pitfalls are left in store for them?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:24.030
I am Midori.

00:23:24.470 --> 00:23:27.720
Midori gets angry, Midori falls in love...

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:28.650
What?

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:31.800
The Ondine Troupe are also performing <i>Takekurabe</i>?

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:38.490
And Ayumi is playing Midori? There's no way I can beat her.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:41.310
But if we don't win, we'll be forced to disband.

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:44.040
What should I do?

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:47.060
Ayumi's Midori is perfect.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 9 - A New Midori

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:49.550
I can't do this!
